<title>CHILE: CHILE NAMES SERGIO JIMENEZ NEW MINING MINISTER.</title>
<headline>CHILE NAMES SERGIO JIMENEZ NEW MINING MINISTER.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Eduardo Frei on Monday named Sergio Jimenez as Chile's new mining minister to replace Benjamin Teplizky who died last week.</p>
<p>Jimenez is currently general manager of Santiago water utility Enmpresa Metropolitana de Obras Sanitarias (Emos).  </p>
<p>Frei made the announcement during a visit to the city of Antofagasta in the northern Second Region.</p>
<p>Jimenez, like Teplizky, is a member of the Radical Party -- one of the smallest parties in the ruling center-left coalition.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
